                <pb facs="0375" n="293" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg293"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.00/937.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Honduran Legation to
                        the Department of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Aide Memoire.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Honduras</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-12-26"><hi rendition="#italic">December 26,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The minister of Honduras presents his compliments to his excellency the Secretary
                    of State and has the honor to inform him <pb facs="0376" n="294" xml:id="pg294"
                    /> that Gens. Manuel Bonilla and Lee Christmas, leaders of the Honduran
                    revolutionists, left New Orleans on Friday the 23d and probably on board the
                    steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Hornet.</hi></p>
            </div>
